//
// Every count `crate::limits::LIMIT` bounds works at exactly 300, on both backends: a struct of
// 300 fields, a function of 300 parameters, a function binding 300 variables, and a tuple of 300
// elements as a literal and as a return type.  Values by hand: fields, parameters and
// variables each hold `i` at position `i` and are summed, 0 + 1 + … + 299 = 44850 (each sum is a
// chain of 299 operators, within the depth limit too); the tuple `(0, 1, …, 299)` has
// `.299 == 299`.  Its refused twins are
// `a-count-past-the-limit-is-refused.loft` and `a-tuple-type-past-the-limit-is-refused.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: none — it pins the limit's lower side; a limit set below 300 fails it with
//   the refusal.

